 activation of the PmrA/PmrB two-component regulatory system of <italic>Salmonella enterica</italic>.</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><volume>63</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17229213</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000233-Vescovi1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vescovi</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name><name><surname>Soncini</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Groisman</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Mg<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> as an extracellular signal: Environmental regulation of <italic>Salmonella</italic> virulence.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>84</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>174</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8548821</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000233-Winfield1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Winfield</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Latifi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Groisman</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Transcriptional regulation of the 4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose biosynthetic genes in <italic>Yersinia pestis</italic>.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>280</volume><fpage>14765</fpage><lpage>14772</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15710615</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000233-Winfield2"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Winfield</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Groisman</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Phenotypic differences between <italic>Salmonella</italic> and <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> resulting from the dispara